From: OpenHarmony PC Developer Community
Subject: [PATCH] Add HarmonyOS system identification to config.guess/config.sub

This patch adds HarmonyOS/OpenHarmony system identification support
to PCRE2's GNU config files (config.guess and config.sub).

HarmonyOS uses `uname -s` returning "HarmonyOS" and requires the
canonical triplet format: aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos

Note: PCRE2 10.40's config.sub already has partial ohos support
(linux-ohos*- in kernel validation), but lacks full recognition.

Related error patterns:
- E007: config.guess cannot guess build type
- E072: config.sub invalid triplet for ohos

Workaround: If config.sub still rejects ohos, use --build=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu

diff --git a/config.guess b/config.guess
--- a/config.guess
+++ b/config.guess
@@ -150,6 +150,11 @@
 
 case $UNAME_SYSTEM in
+HarmonyOS)
+    echo "$UNAME_MACHINE"-unknown-linux-ohos
+    exit ;;
 Linux|GNU|GNU/*)
 	LIBC=unknown
 
diff --git a/config.sub b/config.sub
--- a/config.sub
+++ b/config.sub
@@ -163,6 +163,10 @@
 			android-linux)
 				basic_machine=$field1-unknown
 				basic_os=linux-android
 				;;
+			ohos-linux)
+				basic_machine=$field1-unknown
+				basic_os=linux-ohos
+				;;
 			*)
 				basic_machine=$field1-$field2
 				basic_os=$field3
@@ -1980,6 +1984,7 @@
 	| amigados* \
 	| amigaos* \
 	| android* \
+	| ohos* \
 	| aof* \
 	| aos* \
 	| aros* \